# Atalla 0x01 — Cycle-Accurate Simulator

A cycle-accurate hardware simulator for a heterogeneous SoC accelerator, developed by [Purdue SoCET](https://github.com/Purdue-SoCET/atalla/). Models the full tensor processing datapath — from DRAM through a systolic array — with realistic per-cycle timing for every component.

**Primary use:** measure performance of GEMM and tensor workloads (cycle counts, FLOP rates, memory bandwidth, queue depths) to identify bottlenecks and evaluate scheduling strategies.

> This repository is currently being built.

## Architecture

The simulation engine is gem5-inspired: all components inherit from `Clocked` and execute one `tick()` per cycle, driven by a global `EventQueue`. Inter-component state lives entirely in `SimQueue` FIFOs, so backpressure propagates naturally.

## Repository Layout

```
atalla-sim/
├── src/
│   ├── base/             # Simulation framework (EventQueue, ClockDomain, Clocked)
│   ├── systolic_array/   # SystolicArrayTPU — pipelined grouped MAC engine
│   ├── memory/           # DRAM, Scratchpad, Backend, Crossbar, SRAM banks
│   ├── vector_core/      # VectorCore, VLSU, VectorDatapath, GSAU, Veggie
│   └── atalla/           # System integration, bridges, experiment harnesses
├── tests/                # pytest unit and integration tests
├── tools/                # Sweep runners and visualization scripts
├── docs/                 # Architecture docs, metrics, queue glossary
├── logs/                 # Simulation output (stats, gantt, schedule)
├── Makefile
└── LICENSE               # BSD 3-Clause
```

## Getting Started

```bash
# Run the full test suite
pytest tests/

# Key integration tests
pytest tests/test_scratchpad_vector_core_sysarr_tpu_tiled_1024.py
pytest tests/test_scratchpad_vector_core_sysarr_tpu_tiled_1024_blocked_mn.py

# Parameter sweeps
python tools/run_sysarr_tpu_sweeps.py
python tools/run_blocked_mn_reuse_sweeps.py

# Visualization
python tools/plot_sysarr_tpu_sweeps.py
python tools/plot_blocked_mn_reuse_roofline.py
python tools/plot_tiled_sysarr_tpu_gantt.py
```

Simulation logs are written to `logs/`: `stats.log`, `schedule.log`, `gemm_cycles.log`, `gantt.log`.

